@{
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

<!-- Page hero -->
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container-fluid px-4">
    <h1 class="page-hero-title">About &amp; History</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-subtitle">Over a thousand years of magical education in the heart of Scotland</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- History -->
<section id="history" class="inner-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Our History</h2>
    <div class="row g-4">
      <div class="col-lg-8">
        <p>Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry was founded around 990 A.D. by four of the greatest witches and wizards of the age: Godric Gryffindor, Salazar Slytherin, Rowena Ravenclaw, and Helga Hufflepuff. Together they chose a remote location in the Scottish Highlands, far from Muggle settlements, to establish a school where young witches and wizards could receive a safe and rigorous magical education.</p>
        <p>For over a millennium, Hogwarts has stood as Britain's foremost institution of magical learning. Its enchanted castle, ancient corridors, and moving staircases have sheltered generations of students, guiding them through seven transformative years of study and growth. The school's motto, <em>Draco Dormiens Nunquam Titillandus</em> — "Never Tickle a Sleeping Dragon" — reflects both its wisdom and its wit.</p>
        <p>The early centuries of the school were marked by expansion and consolidation. The library, the greenhouses, and the Astronomy Tower were all established within the first two hundred years. The four founders' original vision — a place of rigorous learning and genuine community — shaped every stone of the castle and every tradition that endures to this day.</p>
        <p>Throughout the centuries, Hogwarts has weathered threats both internal and external. The construction and concealment of the Chamber of Secrets, the imposition of the International Statute of Secrecy, and the dark forces that have periodically tested the wizarding world have each left their mark on the school's fabric and its memory. Each time, the school has endured — restored by the dedication of its staff and the courage of its students.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-4">
        <div class="history-sidebar">
          <h3 class="sidebar-heading">Key Facts</h3>
          <ul class="sidebar-list">
            <li><i class="bi bi-calendar3 me-2"></i>Founded: <strong>c. 990 A.D.</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-geo-alt me-2"></i>Location: <strong>Scottish Highlands</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-mortarboard me-2"></i>Years of Study: <strong>Seven</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-people me-2"></i>Houses: <strong>Four</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-book me-2"></i>Subjects Offered: <strong>Over 20</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-train-front me-2"></i>Access: <strong>Hogwarts Express, Platform 9¾</strong></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-translate me-2"></i>Motto: <strong><em>Draco Dormiens Nunquam Titillandus</em></strong></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Timeline -->
<section id="timeline" class="inner-section inner-section--alt">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Historical Timeline</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Key events in the thousand-year history of Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.</p>
    <div class="timeline">

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">c. 990 A.D.</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">School Founded</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">Godric Gryffindor, Salazar Slytherin, Rowena Ravenclaw, and Helga Hufflepuff establish Hogwarts in the Scottish Highlands. The four founders each select students according to the qualities they most admire.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">c. 993 A.D.</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">Slytherin's Departure</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">Following a bitter dispute over the admission of Muggle-born students, Salazar Slytherin secretly constructs the Chamber of Secrets beneath the school and departs Hogwarts permanently. The chamber remains hidden for nearly a thousand years.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">1692</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">International Statute of Secrecy</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">The International Statute of Wizarding Secrecy is enacted. Hogwarts strengthens its concealment enchantments, rendering the castle invisible to Muggle eyes and unplottable on Muggle maps. The Hogwarts Express is established in the following century to transport students discreetly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">c. 1790</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">Hogwarts Express Established</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">The Ministry of Magic arranges a dedicated steam locomotive service to transport students from London to Hogsmeade Station each September. Platform Nine and Three-Quarters at King's Cross Station is enchanted as the boarding point.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">1943</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">Chamber of Secrets — First Opening</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">The Chamber of Secrets is opened for the first time in a thousand years by sixteen-year-old Tom Marvolo Riddle. Several students are Petrified and one student is killed. Rubeus Hagrid is wrongly blamed and expelled.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-date">1956</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h5 class="timeline-title">Albus Dumbledore Appointed Headmaster</h5>
          <p class="timeline-desc">Professor Albus Dumbledore, widely regarded as the greatest wizard of the age, becomes Headmaster of Hogwarts. His long tenure transforms the school's culture and ensures it remains a place of inclusive magical education.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Founders -->
<section id="founders" class="inner-section inner-section--alt">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">The Four Founders</h2>
    <div class="row g-4">

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="founder-card founder-card--gryffindor">
          <div class="founder-house-badge">Gryffindor</div>
          <h3 class="founder-name">Godric Gryffindor</h3>
          <p class="founder-bio">The most celebrated of the four founders, Gryffindor prized courage, bravery, and nerve above all else. He championed the admission of Muggle-born students and his personal sword — a goblin-made blade set with rubies — became a treasured Hogwarts relic.</p>
          <div class="founder-traits">
            <span class="trait-badge">Courage</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Bravery</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Chivalry</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="founder-card founder-card--slytherin">
          <div class="founder-house-badge">Slytherin</div>
          <h3 class="founder-name">Salazar Slytherin</h3>
          <p class="founder-bio">A Parselmouth and one of the most brilliant wizards of his generation, Slytherin sought students of pure magical heritage. He constructed the Chamber of Secrets beneath the school before departing following a schism with the other founders.</p>
          <div class="founder-traits">
            <span class="trait-badge">Cunning</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Ambition</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Resourcefulness</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="founder-card founder-card--ravenclaw">
          <div class="founder-house-badge">Ravenclaw</div>
          <h3 class="founder-name">Rowena Ravenclaw</h3>
          <p class="founder-bio">Widely regarded as the cleverest of the founders, Ravenclaw valued intelligence, creativity, and wisdom. According to legend, the ingenious layout of Hogwarts castle itself was conceived in a dream she had after following a warty hog to a lake.</p>
          <div class="founder-traits">
            <span class="trait-badge">Wit</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Wisdom</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Creativity</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="founder-card founder-card--hufflepuff">
          <div class="founder-house-badge">Hufflepuff</div>
          <h3 class="founder-name">Helga Hufflepuff</h3>
          <p class="founder-bio">The most inclusive of the four founders, Hufflepuff welcomed students of all backgrounds, valuing hard work, loyalty, and fair play. She also contributed enormously to the school's early community and many of the Hogwarts feast recipes are attributed to her.</p>
          <div class="founder-traits">
            <span class="trait-badge">Loyalty</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Patience</span>
            <span class="trait-badge">Hard Work</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Notable Headmasters -->
<section id="headmasters" class="inner-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Notable Headmasters &amp; Headmistresses</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Hogwarts has been led by many distinguished witches and wizards over its thousand-year history. Their portraits line the Headmaster's office, offering counsel to those who serve after them.</p>
    <div class="row g-4">

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
        <div class="headmaster-card">
          <div class="headmaster-tenure">c. 1200s</div>
          <h5 class="headmaster-name">Eupraxia Mole</h5>
          <p class="headmaster-desc">Negotiated the first formal agreement with the Hogsmeade village residents, establishing the boundaries of school authority and granting students limited access to the village in their later years.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
        <div class="headmaster-card">
          <div class="headmaster-tenure">Late 1800s – Early 1900s</div>
          <h5 class="headmaster-name">Phineas Nigellus Black</h5>
          <p class="headmaster-desc">Widely regarded as the least popular Headmaster in Hogwarts history. A member of the Black family and a proud Slytherin, he governed with strict discipline and little warmth. His portrait remains in the Headmaster's office.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
        <div class="headmaster-card">
          <div class="headmaster-tenure">1930s – 1950s</div>
          <h5 class="headmaster-name">Armando Dippet</h5>
          <p class="headmaster-desc">Headmaster during the years Tom Riddle attended Hogwarts. A mild-mannered and aging wizard, Dippet was deceived by Riddle during the first opening of the Chamber of Secrets and narrowly avoided closing the school.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
        <div class="headmaster-card headmaster-card--featured">
          <div class="headmaster-tenure">1956 – Present</div>
          <h5 class="headmaster-name">Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore</h5>
          <p class="headmaster-desc">Considered the greatest Headmaster in Hogwarts history and by many the greatest wizard of the age. His tenure has transformed the school into a symbol of inclusive magical education and steadfast resistance against the Dark Arts. Defeater of the dark wizard Grindelwald in 1945, he continues to lead Hogwarts with wisdom and care.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Castle -->
<section id="castle" class="inner-section inner-section--alt">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">The Castle</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Hogwarts castle is a vast, many-turreted structure perched on a cliff above the Black Lake, accessible only by magical means or the Hogwarts Express from King's Cross Station, Platform 9¾. The castle is enchanted to appear as a dangerous ruin to Muggle eyes and cannot be located on any Muggle map.</p>
    <div class="row g-4">

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-cup-hot castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">The Great Hall</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">The central gathering place for all students and staff. Its enchanted ceiling reflects the weather above and four long house tables line its floor. Home to the Sorting Ceremony, all communal feasts, and O.W.L. examinations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-book castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">The Library</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">Home to tens of thousands of volumes covering every branch of magic. The Restricted Section requires a signed permission slip from a teacher. Madam Pince has overseen the collection for several decades.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-stars castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">Astronomy Tower</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">The tallest tower of the castle, used exclusively for Astronomy lessons conducted at midnight. Students observe and chart celestial bodies from its open platform using telescopes and enchanted star maps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-trophy castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">Quidditch Pitch</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">A large oval stadium on the castle grounds where inter-house Quidditch matches are played throughout the academic year. Seven tall hooped goal posts stand at each end, surrounded by tiered spectator stands.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-tree castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">The Forbidden Forest</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">A vast, ancient forest bordering the school grounds, home to centaurs, thestrals, unicorns, Acromantulas, and many other magical creatures. Entry is strictly forbidden to students without staff supervision.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-door-open castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">Room of Requirement</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">A hidden chamber on the seventh floor that only appears when a person is in true need of it. The room transforms itself to suit any purpose — a practice space, a hiding place, or a store for objects that need to be concealed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-plus-circle castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">Hospital Wing</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">Located on the first floor, the Hospital Wing is staffed by Madam Pomfrey and treats students for injuries and ailments ranging from Quidditch accidents and hexes to the after-effects of poorly brewed potions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="castle-location-card">
          <i class="bi bi-water castle-location-icon"></i>
          <h4 class="castle-location-name">The Black Lake</h4>
          <p class="castle-location-desc">A deep, cold lake bordering the castle grounds, home to a Giant Squid, Merpeople, Grindylows, and other aquatic creatures. First-year students cross it by boat on the night of their arrival at Hogwarts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
